  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"60b28bea-ca13-1645-aeb5-368f2fbc7c55"],
 "\nYour redefinition \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
             StyleBox["r", "TI"], ",", 
             StyleBox["t", "TI"], ";", 
             StyleBox["L", "TI"]}], ")"}], "\[Tilde]", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["T", "TI"], "-1"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "\\Omega(r,t;L) \\sim T^{-1}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "528517a0-e59a-0443-a828-90f6b35103c5"],
 "\nis one of the best improvements in the whole document. \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"Why it helps\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"94c73efc-929a-3045-9883-10186eeddfdb"],
 "\nYou explicitly solve a dimensional problem: if the theory uses \
exponentials or recursive kernels, then the exponent must be dimensionless. \
So if the kernel looks schematically like \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"exp", "\[NegativeThinSpace]", 
