---\n\n# Important methodological point\n\nA very common failure mode in \
unification attempts is to confuse:\n\n- dimensional consistency,\n- \
numerical coincidence,\n- parameter fitting,\n- symbolic elegance,\n- and \
actual derivation.\n\nRHUFT will become stronger if you explicitly enforce \
these categories.\n\nA formula should be tagged as one of:\n\n- **Dimensional \
identity**\n- **Structural ansatz**\n- **Derived theorem**\n- \
**Phenomenological fit**\n- **Numerical coincidence candidate**\n- \
**Validated prediction**\n\nThat one move would greatly improve the project.\n\
