## RHUFT core statement, cleaner version\n\nRHUFT proposes that the primary \
field variable is a recursive coherence rate $$\\Omega(r,t;L)$$ with \
dimensions $$T^{-1}$$. This permits dimensionally valid self-referential \
kernels and supports an emergent definition of mass as a localized excess of \
integrated coherence contrast over background. In this formulation, the \
coupling required to convert integrated coherence density into mass has the \
same dimensions as $$G^{-1}$$, suggesting that gravitation functions as the \
dimensional scale anchor of mass emergence rather than as an external cause \
of mass itself.\n\nStable particle states are hypothesized to correspond to \
discrete coherent geometric regimes, potentially governed by harmonic and \
self-similar scaling principles. Golden-ratio and related geometric laws are \
explored as candidate organizing structures for mass hierarchy and \
electromagnetic boundary conditions, but these remain conjectural pending \
derivation and predictive validation.\n\nThat is much stronger than the \
current wording because it preserves the insight without overclaiming.\n\n---\
