 "\nIf I were to rewrite RHUFT as rigorously as possible from your material \
so far, I would state it this way: \n",
 Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
    {
     PaneBox[Cell[TextData[{
       "RHUFT is a proposed recursive coherence-based field framework in \
which localized physical structure is modeled as emergent from contrastive \
organization of a background field. A mathematically consistent formulation \
is obtained if the primary field variable is treated as a rate-like quantity \
with dimensions ",
       Cell[BoxData[
        FormBox[
         TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
             SuperscriptBox[
              StyleBox["T", "TI"], "-1"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
           "input" -> "T^{-1}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
          "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
        "a44a1321-9f39-fc47-a275-de8ccfdae854"],
       ", enabling dimensionless recursive kernels. Under a natural mass \
ansatz in which mass is proportional to integrated quadratic coherence \
contrast over spatial support, the required coupling has the same dimensions \
as ",
       Cell[BoxData[
        FormBox[
         TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
             SuperscriptBox[
              StyleBox["G", "TI"], "-1"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
           "input" -> "G^{-1}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
          "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
        "2e631aec-2b89-d248-87d6-eb0f410d0e42"],
       ", suggesting a deep relation between gravitation-scale dimensionality \
and emergent mass. Additional hypotheses propose that stable matter may \
occupy discrete coherent geometric regimes and that hierarchy may reflect \
harmonic or self-similar scaling, but these latter claims remain conjectural \
pending derivation and predictive validation."
      }],
