\\n## 4. Summary by Category\\n\\n```wl\\nNormal @ \
Counts[rhuftClaimAudit[All, \\\"Category\\\"] // \
Normal]\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nclaimCategorySummary = Dataset @ KeyValueMap[\\n   \
<|\\\"Category\\\" -> #1, \\\"Count\\\" -> #2|> &,\\n   Normal @ \
Counts[rhuftClaimAudit[All, \\\"Category\\\"] // \
Normal]\\n];\\n\\nclaimCategorySummary\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Audit \
Utilities\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[\\n   claimsByCategory,\\n   claimsByType,\\n \
  claimsByLayer,\\n   claimRiskRegister,\\n   claimActionRegister,\\n   \
claimDashboard\\n];\\n\\nclaimsByCategory[data_Dataset, category_String] \
:=\\n   data[Select[#Category == category \
&]];\\n\\nclaimsByType[data_Dataset, type_String] :=\\n   data[Select[#Type \
== type &]];\\n\\nclaimsByLayer[data_Dataset, layer_String] :=\\n   \
data[Select[#RHUFTLayer == layer &]];\\n\\nclaimRiskRegister[data_Dataset] :=\
\\n   data[All, {\\\"ID\\\", \\\"Claim\\\", \\\"Category\\\", \\\"Risk\\\"}];\
\\n\\nclaimActionRegister[data_Dataset] :=\\n   data[All, {\\\"ID\\\", \
\\\"Claim\\\", \\\"Category\\\", \
\\\"NextAction\\\"}];\\n\\nclaimDashboard[data_Dataset] := Module[\\n   {\\n  \
    categoryCounts,\\n      barChart\\n   },\\n   categoryCounts = \
Counts[data[All, \\\"Category\\\"] // Normal];\\n   barChart = BarChart[\\n   \
   Lookup[categoryCounts, claimStatusLevels, 0],\\n      ChartLabels -> \
claimStatusLevels,\\n      ChartStyle -> (claimStatusStyle /@ \
claimStatusLevels),\\n      ImageSize -> Large,\\n      PlotLabel -> \
\\\"RHUFT Claim Audit Overview\\\"\\n   ];\\n   Column[{\\n      \
Style[\\\"RHUFT Claim Audit Dashboard\\\", 16, Bold],\\n      barChart,\\n    \
  Dataset @ KeyValueMap[\\n         <|\\\"Category\\\" -> #1, \\\"Count\\\" \
-> #2|> &,\\n         categoryCounts\\n      ]\\n   }]\\n];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\
\\n## 6. Example Queries\\n\\n### Claims currently treated as \
Derived\\n\\n```wl\\nclaimsByCategory[rhuftClaimAudit, \\\"Derived\\\"]\\n```\
\\n\\n### Claims that need evidence most \
urgently\\n\\n```wl\\nclaimsByCategory[rhuftClaimAudit, \
\\\"NeedsEvidence\\\"]\\n```\\n\\n### All numerical-fit style \
claims\\n\\n```wl\\nclaimsByType[rhuftClaimAudit, \\\"NumericalFit\\\"]\\n```\
\\n\\n### Risk register\\n\\n```wl\\nclaimRiskRegister[rhuftClaimAudit]\\n```\
\\n\\n### Action \
register\\n\\n```wl\\nclaimActionRegister[rhuftClaimAudit]\\n```\\n\\n### \
Dashboard\\n\\n```wl\\nclaimDashboard[rhuftClaimAudit]\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \
7. Professional Review Rules\\n\\n```wl\\nreviewRules = Dataset @ {\\n   <|\\\
\"Rule\\\" -> \\\"No dimensional result may be presented as a physical \
identity without additional derivation.\\\", \\\"Priority\\\" -> \\\"Critical\
\\\"|>,\\n   <|\\\"Rule\\\" -> \\\"No numerical agreement may be called proof \
if correction factors are introduced post hoc.\\\", \\\"Priority\\\" -> \
\\\"Critical\\\"|>,\\n   <|\\\"Rule\\\" -> \\\"All interpretive language must \
be separable from the underlying formal claim.\\\", \\\"Priority\\\" -> \
\\\"High\\\"|>,\\n   <|\\\"Rule\\\" -> \\\"Every claim in RHUFT should have \
an explicit validation path.\\\", \\\"Priority\\\" -> \\\"High\\\"|>,\\n   <|\
\\\"Rule\\\" -> \\\"Golden-ratio and geometric claims must be compared \
against alternative baselines.\\\", \\\"Priority\\\" -> \\\"High\\\"|>,\\n   \
<|\\\"Rule\\\" -> \\\"Master equations must display factor confidence levels \
explicitly.\\\", \\\"Priority\\\" -> \
\\\"High\\\"|>\\n};\\n\\nreviewRules\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Recommended \
Next Actions\\n\\n```wl\\nnextProfessionalActions = Dataset @ {\\n   \
<|\\\"Step\\\" -> 1, \\\"Action\\\" -> \\\"Formalize \[CapitalOmega] as a \
precise mathematical object with units, domain, and update law.\\\", \
\\\"Outcome\\\" -> \\\"Reduces ambiguity in the field foundation.\\\"|>,\\n   \
<|\\\"Step\\\" -> 2, \\\"Action\\\" -> \\\"Rewrite the mass-emergence section \
to separate dimensional derivation from physical identification.\\\", \
\\\"Outcome\\\" -> \\\"Prevents overclaiming around G^-1.\\\"|>,\\n   \
<|\\\"Step\\\" -> 3, \\\"Action\\\" -> \\\"Move the proton/electron ratio \
formula into a candidate-identity appendix until independently derived.\\\", \
\\\"Outcome\\\" -> \\\"Improves theoretical credibility.\\\"|>,\\n   \
<|\\\"Step\\\" -> 4, \\\"Action\\\" -> \\\"Reframe the fine-structure \
discussion as an idealized ansatz plus residual diagnostic.\\\", \
\\\"Outcome\\\" -> \\\"Avoids treating mismatch as proof.\\\"|>,\\n   \
<|\\\"Step\\\" -> 5, \\\"Action\\\" -> \\\"Create a companion validation \
notebook comparing RHUFT scaling claims against null and alternative \
models.\\\", \\\"Outcome\\\" -> \\\"Makes RHUFT ablation-ready and \
falsifiable.\\\"|>,\\n   <|\\\"Step\\\" -> 6, \\\"Action\\\" -> \\\"Adopt \
this claim-audit dataset as the canonical governance layer for all future \
RHUFT revisions.\\\", \\\"Outcome\\\" -> \\\"Establishes professional \
documentation \
discipline.\\\"|>\\n};\\n\\nnextProfessionalActions\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. \
Optional Extension: Confidence \
Scores\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[withConfidenceScore];\\n\\nwithConfidenceScore[\
data_Dataset] := Dataset @ Map[\\n   Append[\\n      #,\\n      \
\\\"ConfidenceScore\\\" -> Switch[#Category,\\n         \\\"Derived\\\", 0.9,\
\\n         \\\"Provisional\\\", 0.6,\\n         \\\"Speculative\\\", \
0.35,\\n         \\\"NeedsEvidence\\\", 0.2,\\n         _, \
Missing[\\\"Unknown\\\"]\\n      ]\\n   ] &,\\n   \
Normal[data]\\n];\\n\\nwithConfidenceScore[rhuftClaimAudit]\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\
\\n## Closing Note\\n\\nThis notebook is designed to become the professional \
governance layer for RHUFT development.\\n\\nIts function is to ensure that \
RHUFT evolves with:\\n\\n- dimensional rigor,\\n- claim traceability,\\n- \
separation of derivation from interpretation,\\n- numerical honesty,\\n- and \
a clear validation roadmap.\\n\\nThe intended result is not merely a stronger \
document, but a stronger research program.\"\>",
                    Background->None,
                    FrameMargins->1,
                    FrameStyle->Dynamic[
                    CurrentValue[Background]],
                    StripOnInput->False], True->
                    FrameBox[
                    
                    StyleBox["\<\"# RHUFT Claim Audit Notebook\\n\\n## \
Purpose\\n\\nThis notebook provides a professional claim-audit framework for \
the current RHUFT material. Its goal is to distinguish:\\n\\n1. \
**Derived**\\n2. **Provisional**\\n3. **Speculative**\\n4. **Needs Evidence**\
\\n\\nThe purpose is not to weaken RHUFT, but to strengthen it by separating:\
\\n\\n- dimensional results,\\n- structural modeling choices,\\n- conjectural \
scaling laws,\\n- numerical fits,\\n- and empirically unsupported \
interpretive claims.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Audit \
Categories\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[claimStatusLevels, claimStatusStyle, \
claimStatusOrder];\\n\\nclaimStatusLevels = {\\n   \\\"Derived\\\",\\n   \
\\\"Provisional\\\",\\n   \\\"Speculative\\\",\\n   \
\\\"NeedsEvidence\\\"\\n};\\n\\nclaimStatusOrder = \
AssociationThread[claimStatusLevels, \
Range[Length[claimStatusLevels]]];\\n\\nclaimStatusStyle = <|\\n   \
\\\"Derived\\\" -> Darker[Green, 0.2],\\n   \\\"Provisional\\\" -> \
RGBColor[0.85, 0.55, 0.1],\\n   \\\"Speculative\\\" -> RGBColor[0.75, 0.25, \
0.2],\\n   \\\"NeedsEvidence\\\" -> \
GrayLevel[0.35]\\n|>;\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Audit \
Schema\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[rhuftClaimSchema];\\n\\nrhuftClaimSchema = {\\n  \
 \\\"ID\\\",\\n   \\\"Claim\\\",\\n   \\\"Equation\\\",\\n   \
\\\"Category\\\",\\n   \\\"Type\\\",\\n   \\\"RHUFTLayer\\\",\\n   \
\\\"Rationale\\\",\\n   \\\"Dependencies\\\",\\n   \\\"Evidence\\\",\\n   \
\\\"ValidationPath\\\",\\n   \\\"Risk\\\",\\n   \
\\\"NextAction\\\"\\n};\\n\\nrhuftClaimSchema\\n```\\n\\n### Field \
meanings\\n\\n- `ID`: stable identifier for cross-reference\\n- `Claim`: \
concise statement of the claim\\n- `Equation`: symbolic or textual equation \
associated with the claim\\n- `Category`: one of `\\\"Derived\\\"`, \
`\\\"Provisional\\\"`, `\\\"Speculative\\\"`, `\\\"NeedsEvidence\\\"`\\n- \
`Type`: e.g. `\\\"Dimensional\\\"`, `\\\"Structural\\\"`, \
`\\\"Phenomenological\\\"`, `\\\"Interpretive\\\"`, \
`\\\"NumericalFit\\\"`\\n- `RHUFTLayer`: architectural layer or conceptual \
region\\n- `Rationale`: why the current category is assigned\\n- \
`Dependencies`: assumptions required for the claim\\n- `Evidence`: current \
support already available\\n- `ValidationPath`: how to test or derive further\
\\n- `Risk`: what could fail or be misleading\\n- `NextAction`: professional \
next step\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Initial RHUFT Claim Audit \
Dataset\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[rhuftClaimAudit];\\n\\nrhuftClaimAudit = \
Dataset @ {\\n   <|\\n      \\\"ID\\\" -> \\\"RHUFT-C001\\\",\\n      \
\\\"Claim\\\" -> \\\"The primary field variable can be defined as a recursive \
coherence rate \[CapitalOmega] with dimensions T^-1.\\\",\\n      \
\\\"Equation\\\" -> HoldForm[\[CapitalOmega][r, t, L]],\\n      \
\\\"Category\\\" -> \\\"Provisional\\\",\\n      \\\"Type\\\" -> \
\\\"Structural\\\",\\n      \\\"RHUFTLayer\\\" -> \\\"Field \
Foundation\\\",\\n      \\\"Rationale\\\" -> \\\"A coherent dimensional \
correction that resolves exponent arguments, but still depends on RHUFT's \
chosen field interpretation.\\\",\\n      \\\"Dependencies\\\" -> \
{\\\"Recursive field formulation\\\", \\\"Kernel-based self-reference\\\", \\\
\"Time-like sampling interpretation\\\"},\\n      \\\"Evidence\\\" -> \
{\\\"Dimensionally consistent with kernel arguments of the form \[Lambda] \
\[CapitalOmega] ds\\\"},\\n      \\\"ValidationPath\\\" -> {\\\"Formalize \
\[CapitalOmega] operationally\\\", \\\"Derive all downstream equations using \
\[CapitalOmega]\\\", \\\"Show no dimensional contradictions remain\\\"},\\n   \
