ansatz but not uniquely derived from first principles.\\\",\\n      \
\\\"Dependencies\\\" -> {\\\"Background-relative ontology\\\", \\\"Quadratic \
contrast density\\\", \\\"Effective particle support volume\\\"},\\n      \
\\\"Evidence\\\" -> {\\\"Conceptually coherent\\\", \\\"Compatible with \
energy-density style constructions\\\"},\\n      \\\"ValidationPath\\\" -> \
{\\\"Derive from variational principle or stability condition\\\", \
\\\"Compare with alternative functionals\\\"},\\n      \\\"Risk\\\" -> \
\\\"May be one of many possible functionals; current form is not uniquely \
justified.\\\",\\n      \\\"NextAction\\\" -> \\\"Compare quadratic, linear, \
and invariant-based contrast formulations.\\\"\\n   |>,\\n   <|\\n      \
\\\"ID\\\" -> \\\"RHUFT-C004\\\",\\n      \\\"Claim\\\" -> \\\"The \
mass-coupling coefficient required by the coherence-contrast integral has the \
dimensions of G^-1.\\\",\\n      \\\"Equation\\\" -> \
HoldForm[Dimensions[Cmass] == Dimensions[1/G]],\\n      \\\"Category\\\" -> \
\\\"Derived\\\",\\n      \\\"Type\\\" -> \\\"Dimensional\\\",\\n      \
\\\"RHUFTLayer\\\" -> \\\"Mass Emergence\\\",\\n      \\\"Rationale\\\" -> \\\
\"Direct dimensional analysis yields M L^-3 T^2, matching G^-1.\\\",\\n      \
\\\"Dependencies\\\" -> {\\\"Mass functional form\\\", \\\"\[CapitalOmega] \
has units T^-1\\\", \\\"Volume integration in L^3\\\"},\\n      \
\\\"Evidence\\\" -> {\\\"Explicit dimensional calculation\\\"},\\n      \
\\\"ValidationPath\\\" -> {\\\"Reproduce symbolically\\\", \\\"Confirm under \
alternate notation and units\\\"},\\n      \\\"Risk\\\" -> \\\"Only as strong \
as the assumed functional form.\\\",\\n      \\\"NextAction\\\" -> \\\"Keep \
as a dimensional result, not yet as a physical identity.\\\"\\n   |>,\\n   <|\
\\n      \\\"ID\\\" -> \\\"RHUFT-C005\\\",\\n      \\\"Claim\\\" -> \\\"The \
physical coupling in the mass emergence equation is exactly G^-1.\\\",\\n     \
 \\\"Equation\\\" -> HoldForm[Cmass == 1/G],\\n      \\\"Category\\\" -> \
\\\"NeedsEvidence\\\",\\n      \\\"Type\\\" -> \\\"Interpretive\\\",\\n      \
\\\"RHUFTLayer\\\" -> \\\"Mass Emergence\\\",\\n      \\\"Rationale\\\" -> \\\
\"Dimensional compatibility alone does not prove exact physical \
identity.\\\",\\n      \\\"Dependencies\\\" -> {\\\"Claim RHUFT functional is \
physically realized\\\", \\\"No missing dimensionless prefactor\\\", \\\"No \
alternate coupling scale\\\"},\\n      \\\"Evidence\\\" -> {\\\"Dimensional \
match only\\\"},\\n      \\\"ValidationPath\\\" -> {\\\"Derive from deeper \
field equation\\\", \\\"Constrain via observable predictions\\\", \\\"Check \
whether a dimensionless factor is required\\\"},\\n      \\\"Risk\\\" -> \
\\\"Overclaiming dimensional analysis as ontology.\\\",\\n      \
\\\"NextAction\\\" -> \\\"Restate as a hypothesis until derived or \
independently constrained.\\\"\\n   |>,\\n   <|\\n      \\\"ID\\\" -> \
\\\"RHUFT-C006\\\",\\n      \\\"Claim\\\" -> \\\"Particle mass ratios follow \
a golden-ratio harmonic scaling law \[CurlyPhi]^\[CapitalDelta]n.\\\",\\n     \
 \\\"Equation\\\" -> HoldForm[MB/MA \.7f \[CurlyPhi]^\[CapitalDelta]n],\\n    \
  \\\"Category\\\" -> \\\"Speculative\\\",\\n      \\\"Type\\\" -> \
\\\"Phenomenological\\\",\\n      \\\"RHUFTLayer\\\" -> \\\"Geometric \
Hierarchy\\\",\\n      \\\"Rationale\\\" -> \\\"Interesting organizational \
hypothesis, but not derived in the current material.\\\",\\n      \
