                    "# RHUFT Claim Audit Notebook\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis \
notebook provides a professional claim-audit framework for the current RHUFT \
material. Its goal is to distinguish:\n\n1. **Derived**\n2. **Provisional**\n\
3. **Speculative**\n4. **Needs Evidence**\n\nThe purpose is not to weaken \
RHUFT, but to strengthen it by separating:\n\n- dimensional results,\n- \
structural modeling choices,\n- conjectural scaling laws,\n- numerical fits,\n\
- and empirically unsupported interpretive claims.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Audit \
Categories\n\n```wl\nClearAll[claimStatusLevels, claimStatusStyle, \
claimStatusOrder];\n\nclaimStatusLevels = {\n   \"Derived\",\n   \
\"Provisional\",\n   \"Speculative\",\n   \"NeedsEvidence\"\n};\n\n\
claimStatusOrder = AssociationThread[claimStatusLevels, \
Range[Length[claimStatusLevels]]];\n\nclaimStatusStyle = <|\n   \"Derived\" \
-> Darker[Green, 0.2],\n   \"Provisional\" -> RGBColor[0.85, 0.55, 0.1],\n   \
\"Speculative\" -> RGBColor[0.75, 0.25, 0.2],\n   \"NeedsEvidence\" -> \
GrayLevel[0.35]\n|>;\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Audit Schema\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[rhuftClaimSchema];\n\nrhuftClaimSchema = {\n   \"ID\",\n   \
\"Claim\",\n   \"Equation\",\n   \"Category\",\n   \"Type\",\n   \"RHUFTLayer\
\",\n   \"Rationale\",\n   \"Dependencies\",\n   \"Evidence\",\n   \
\"ValidationPath\",\n   \"Risk\",\n   \"NextAction\"\n};\n\nrhuftClaimSchema\n\
```\n\n### Field meanings\n\n- `ID`: stable identifier for cross-reference\n- \
`Claim`: concise statement of the claim\n- `Equation`: symbolic or textual \
equation associated with the claim\n- `Category`: one of `\"Derived\"`, \
`\"Provisional\"`, `\"Speculative\"`, `\"NeedsEvidence\"`\n- `Type`: e.g. \
`\"Dimensional\"`, `\"Structural\"`, `\"Phenomenological\"`, \
`\"Interpretive\"`, `\"NumericalFit\"`\n- `RHUFTLayer`: architectural layer \
or conceptual region\n- `Rationale`: why the current category is assigned\n- \
`Dependencies`: assumptions required for the claim\n- `Evidence`: current \
support already available\n- `ValidationPath`: how to test or derive further\n\
- `Risk`: what could fail or be misleading\n- `NextAction`: professional next \
step\n\n---\n\n## 3. Initial RHUFT Claim Audit Dataset\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[rhuftClaimAudit];\n\nrhuftClaimAudit = Dataset @ {\n   <|\n      \
\"ID\" -> \"RHUFT-C001\",\n      \"Claim\" -> \"The primary field variable \
can be defined as a recursive coherence rate \[CapitalOmega] with dimensions \
T^-1.\",\n      \"Equation\" -> HoldForm[\[CapitalOmega][r, t, L]],\n      \
\"Category\" -> \"Provisional\",\n      \"Type\" -> \"Structural\",\n      \
\"RHUFTLayer\" -> \"Field Foundation\",\n      \"Rationale\" -> \"A coherent \
dimensional correction that resolves exponent arguments, but still depends on \
RHUFT's chosen field interpretation.\",\n      \"Dependencies\" -> \
{\"Recursive field formulation\", \"Kernel-based self-reference\", \
