      "# RHUFT Claim Audit Notebook\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis notebook provides a \
professional claim-audit framework for the current RHUFT material. Its goal \
is to distinguish:\n\n1. **Derived**\n2. **Provisional**\n3. **Speculative**\n\
4. **Needs Evidence**\n\nThe purpose is not to weaken RHUFT, but to \
strengthen it by separating:\n\n- dimensional results,\n- structural modeling \
choices,\n- conjectural scaling laws,\n- numerical fits,\n- and empirically \
unsupported interpretive claims.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Audit Categories\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[claimStatusLevels, claimStatusStyle, claimStatusOrder];\n\n\
claimStatusLevels = {\n   \"Derived\",\n   \"Provisional\",\n   \"Speculative\
\",\n   \"NeedsEvidence\"\n};\n\nclaimStatusOrder = \
AssociationThread[claimStatusLevels, Range[Length[claimStatusLevels]]];\n\n\
claimStatusStyle = <|\n   \"Derived\" -> Darker[Green, 0.2],\n   \
\"Provisional\" -> RGBColor[0.85, 0.55, 0.1],\n   \"Speculative\" -> \
RGBColor[0.75, 0.25, 0.2],\n   \"NeedsEvidence\" -> GrayLevel[0.35]\n|>;\n```\
\n\n---\n\n## 2. Audit Schema\n\n```wl\nClearAll[rhuftClaimSchema];\n\n\
rhuftClaimSchema = {\n   \"ID\",\n   \"Claim\",\n   \"Equation\",\n   \
\"Category\",\n   \"Type\",\n   \"RHUFTLayer\",\n   \"Rationale\",\n   \
\"Dependencies\",\n   \"Evidence\",\n   \"ValidationPath\",\n   \"Risk\",\n   \
\"NextAction\"\n};\n\nrhuftClaimSchema\n```\n\n### Field meanings\n\n- `ID`: \
stable identifier for cross-reference\n- `Claim`: concise statement of the \
claim\n- `Equation`: symbolic or textual equation associated with the claim\n\
- `Category`: one of `\"Derived\"`, `\"Provisional\"`, `\"Speculative\"`, \
`\"NeedsEvidence\"`\n- `Type`: e.g. `\"Dimensional\"`, `\"Structural\"`, \
`\"Phenomenological\"`, `\"Interpretive\"`, `\"NumericalFit\"`\n- \
`RHUFTLayer`: architectural layer or conceptual region\n- `Rationale`: why \
the current category is assigned\n- `Dependencies`: assumptions required for \
the claim\n- `Evidence`: current support already available\n- \
`ValidationPath`: how to test or derive further\n- `Risk`: what could fail or \
be misleading\n- `NextAction`: professional next step\n\n---\n\n## 3. Initial \
RHUFT Claim Audit Dataset\n\n```wl\nClearAll[rhuftClaimAudit];\n\n\
rhuftClaimAudit = Dataset @ {\n   <|\n      \"ID\" -> \"RHUFT-C001\",\n      \
\"Claim\" -> \"The primary field variable can be defined as a recursive \
coherence rate \[CapitalOmega] with dimensions T^-1.\",\n      \"Equation\" \
-> HoldForm[\[CapitalOmega][r, t, L]],\n      \"Category\" -> \
\"Provisional\",\n      \"Type\" -> \"Structural\",\n      \"RHUFTLayer\" -> \
\"Field Foundation\",\n      \"Rationale\" -> \"A coherent dimensional \
correction that resolves exponent arguments, but still depends on RHUFT's \
chosen field interpretation.\",\n      \"Dependencies\" -> {\"Recursive field \
formulation\", \"Kernel-based self-reference\", \"Time-like sampling \
interpretation\"},\n      \"Evidence\" -> {\"Dimensionally consistent with \
kernel arguments of the form \[Lambda] \[CapitalOmega] ds\"},\n      \
\"ValidationPath\" -> {\"Formalize \[CapitalOmega] operationally\", \"Derive \
all downstream equations using \[CapitalOmega]\", \"Show no dimensional \
contradictions remain\"},\n      \"Risk\" -> \"Interpretive ambiguity between \
frequency, coherence, and information-processing language.\",\n      \
\"NextAction\" -> \"Define \[CapitalOmega] precisely as a measurable or \
computable field quantity.\"\n   |>,\n   <|\n      \"ID\" -> \"RHUFT-C002\",\n\
      \"Claim\" -> \"The argument of a recursive exponential kernel must be \
dimensionless.\",\n      \"Equation\" -> HoldForm[\[Lambda] \[CapitalOmega] \
ds],\n      \"Category\" -> \"Derived\",\n      \"Type\" -> \"Dimensional\",\n\
      \"RHUFTLayer\" -> \"Mathematical Consistency\",\n      \"Rationale\" -> \
\"This is a standard dimensional requirement for exponential arguments.\",\n  \
    \"Dependencies\" -> {\"Use of exponential kernel\"},\n      \"Evidence\" \
