  "CellToStringData" -> 
   "/create_nb\n# RHUFT Claim Audit Notebook\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis notebook \
provides a professional claim-audit framework for the current RHUFT material. \
Its goal is to distinguish:\n\n1. **Derived**\n2. **Provisional**\n3. \
**Speculative**\n4. **Needs Evidence**\n\nThe purpose is not to weaken RHUFT, \
but to strengthen it by separating:\n\n- dimensional results,\n- structural \
modeling choices,\n- conjectural scaling laws,\n- numerical fits,\n- and \
empirically unsupported interpretive claims.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Audit Categories\
\n\n```wl\nClearAll[claimStatusLevels, claimStatusStyle, claimStatusOrder];\n\
\nclaimStatusLevels = {\n   \"Derived\",\n   \"Provisional\",\n   \
\"Speculative\",\n   \"NeedsEvidence\"\n};\n\nclaimStatusOrder = \
AssociationThread[claimStatusLevels, Range[Length[claimStatusLevels]]];\n\n\
claimStatusStyle = <|\n   \"Derived\" -> Darker[Green, 0.2],\n   \
\"Provisional\" -> RGBColor[0.85, 0.55, 0.1],\n   \"Speculative\" -> \
RGBColor[0.75, 0.25, 0.2],\n   \"NeedsEvidence\" -> GrayLevel[0.35]\n|>;\n```\
\n\n---\n\n## 2. Audit Schema\n\n```wl\nClearAll[rhuftClaimSchema];\n\n\
rhuftClaimSchema = {\n   \"ID\",\n   \"Claim\",\n   \"Equation\",\n   \
\"Category\",\n   \"Type\",\n   \"RHUFTLayer\",\n   \"Rationale\",\n   \
\"Dependencies\",\n   \"Evidence\",\n   \"ValidationPath\",\n   \"Risk\",\n   \
\"NextAction\"\n};\n\nrhuftClaimSchema\n```\n\n### Field meanings\n\n- `ID`: \
stable identifier for cross-reference\n- `Claim`: concise statement of the \
claim\n- `Equation`: symbolic or textual equation associated with the claim\n\
- `Category`: one of `\"Derived\"`, `\"Provisional\"`, `\"Speculative\"`, \
`\"NeedsEvidence\"`\n- `Type`: e.g. `\"Dimensional\"`, `\"Structural\"`, \
`\"Phenomenological\"`, `\"Interpretive\"`, `\"NumericalFit\"`\n- \
`RHUFTLayer`: architectural layer or conceptual region\n- `Rationale`: why \
the current category is assigned\n- `Dependencies`: assumptions required for \
the claim\n- `Evidence`: current support already available\n- \
`ValidationPath`: how to test or derive further\n- `Risk`: what could fail or \
be misleading\n- `NextAction`: professional next step\n\n---\n\n## 3. Initial \
RHUFT Claim Audit Dataset\n\n```wl\nClearAll[rhuftClaimAudit];\n\n\
rhuftClaimAudit = Dataset @ {\n   <|\n      \"ID\" -> \"RHUFT-C001\",\n      \
\"Claim\" -> \"The primary field variable can be defined as a recursive \
coherence rate \[CapitalOmega] with dimensions T^-1.\",\n      \"Equation\" \
-> HoldForm[\[CapitalOmega][r, t, L]],\n      \"Category\" -> \
\"Provisional\",\n      \"Type\" -> \"Structural\",\n      \"RHUFTLayer\" -> \
\"Field Foundation\",\n      \"Rationale\" -> \"A coherent dimensional \
correction that resolves exponent arguments, but still depends on RHUFT's \
chosen field interpretation.\",\n      \"Dependencies\" -> {\"Recursive field \
formulation\", \"Kernel-based self-reference\", \"Time-like sampling \
interpretation\"},\n      \"Evidence\" -> {\"Dimensionally consistent with \
kernel arguments of the form \[Lambda] \[CapitalOmega] ds\"},\n      \
\"ValidationPath\" -> {\"Formalize \[CapitalOmega] operationally\", \"Derive \
all downstream equations using \[CapitalOmega]\", \"Show no dimensional \
contradictions remain\"},\n      \"Risk\" -> \"Interpretive ambiguity between \
frequency, coherence, and information-processing language.\",\n      \
\"NextAction\" -> \"Define \[CapitalOmega] precisely as a measurable or \
computable field quantity.\"\n   |>,\n   <|\n      \"ID\" -> \"RHUFT-C002\",\n\
      \"Claim\" -> \"The argument of a recursive exponential kernel must be \
dimensionless.\",\n      \"Equation\" -> HoldForm[\[Lambda] \[CapitalOmega] \
ds],\n      \"Category\" -> \"Derived\",\n      \"Type\" -> \"Dimensional\",\n\
      \"RHUFTLayer\" -> \"Mathematical Consistency\",\n      \"Rationale\" -> \
\"This is a standard dimensional requirement for exponential arguments.\",\n  \
    \"Dependencies\" -> {\"Use of exponential kernel\"},\n      \"Evidence\" \
-> {\"General mathematical rule for exponentials\"},\n      \
\"ValidationPath\" -> {\"Check all RHUFT kernels for dimensional closure\"},\n\
      \"Risk\" -> \"Low; only fails if the kernel form is changed.\",\n      \
\"NextAction\" -> \"Audit every recursion/exponential term in RHUFT for \
dimensional correctness.\"\n   |>,\n   <|\n      \"ID\" -> \"RHUFT-C003\",\n  \
    \"Claim\" -> \"Mass can be modeled as an integrated coherence-contrast \
functional relative to a background field.\",\n      \"Equation\" -> \
HoldForm[M == Cmass Integrate[Abs[\[CapitalOmega]rec]^2 - \
Abs[\[CapitalOmega]base]^2, {r, Vol}]],\n      \"Category\" -> \
\"Provisional\",\n      \"Type\" -> \"Structural\",\n      \"RHUFTLayer\" -> \
\"Mass Emergence\",\n      \"Rationale\" -> \"This is a plausible RHUFT \
ansatz but not uniquely derived from first principles.\",\n      \
\"Dependencies\" -> {\"Background-relative ontology\", \"Quadratic contrast \
density\", \"Effective particle support volume\"},\n      \"Evidence\" -> \
{\"Conceptually coherent\", \"Compatible with energy-density style \
constructions\"},\n      \"ValidationPath\" -> {\"Derive from variational \
principle or stability condition\", \"Compare with alternative \
functionals\"},\n      \"Risk\" -> \"May be one of many possible functionals; \
current form is not uniquely justified.\",\n      \"NextAction\" -> \"Compare \
quadratic, linear, and invariant-based contrast formulations.\"\n   |>,\n   \
<|\n      \"ID\" -> \"RHUFT-C004\",\n      \"Claim\" -> \"The mass-coupling \
coefficient required by the coherence-contrast integral has the dimensions of \
G^-1.\",\n      \"Equation\" -> HoldForm[Dimensions[Cmass] == \
Dimensions[1/G]],\n      \"Category\" -> \"Derived\",\n      \"Type\" -> \
\"Dimensional\",\n      \"RHUFTLayer\" -> \"Mass Emergence\",\n      \
\"Rationale\" -> \"Direct dimensional analysis yields M L^-3 T^2, matching \
G^-1.\",\n      \"Dependencies\" -> {\"Mass functional form\", \"\
\[CapitalOmega] has units T^-1\", \"Volume integration in L^3\"},\n      \
\"Evidence\" -> {\"Explicit dimensional calculation\"},\n      \
\"ValidationPath\" -> {\"Reproduce symbolically\", \"Confirm under alternate \
notation and units\"},\n      \"Risk\" -> \"Only as strong as the assumed \
functional form.\",\n      \"NextAction\" -> \"Keep as a dimensional result, \
not yet as a physical identity.\"\n   |>,\n   <|\n      \"ID\" -> \
\"RHUFT-C005\",\n      \"Claim\" -> \"The physical coupling in the mass \
emergence equation is exactly G^-1.\",\n      \"Equation\" -> HoldForm[Cmass \
== 1/G],\n      \"Category\" -> \"NeedsEvidence\",\n      \"Type\" -> \
\"Interpretive\",\n      \"RHUFTLayer\" -> \"Mass Emergence\",\n      \
\"Rationale\" -> \"Dimensional compatibility alone does not prove exact \
physical identity.\",\n      \"Dependencies\" -> {\"Claim RHUFT functional is \
physically realized\", \"No missing dimensionless prefactor\", \"No alternate \
coupling scale\"},\n      \"Evidence\" -> {\"Dimensional match only\"},\n     \
 \"ValidationPath\" -> {\"Derive from deeper field equation\", \"Constrain \
via observable predictions\", \"Check whether a dimensionless factor is \
required\"},\n      \"Risk\" -> \"Overclaiming dimensional analysis as \
ontology.\",\n      \"NextAction\" -> \"Restate as a hypothesis until derived \
or independently constrained.\"\n   |>,\n   <|\n      \"ID\" -> \
\"RHUFT-C006\",\n      \"Claim\" -> \"Particle mass ratios follow a \
golden-ratio harmonic scaling law \[CurlyPhi]^\[CapitalDelta]n.\",\n      \
\"Equation\" -> HoldForm[MB/MA \.7f \[CurlyPhi]^\[CapitalDelta]n],\n      \
\"Category\" -> \"Speculative\",\n      \"Type\" -> \"Phenomenological\",\n   \
   \"RHUFTLayer\" -> \"Geometric Hierarchy\",\n      \"Rationale\" -> \
\"Interesting organizational hypothesis, but not derived in the current \
material.\",\n      \"Dependencies\" -> {\"Discrete harmonic state model\", \
\"Golden-ratio privileged scaling\", \"Particle-family state assignment\"},\n \
     \"Evidence\" -> {\"Motivated by self-similar geometric intuition\"},\n   \
   \"ValidationPath\" -> {\"Define state index n rigorously\", \"Test across \
multiple particle ratios\", \"Compare against non-\[CurlyPhi] \
alternatives\"},\n      \"Risk\" -> \"Can collapse into numerology if not \
independently derived.\",\n      \"NextAction\" -> \"Build a comparative \
particle-ratio study against alternative scaling bases.\"\n   |>,\n   <|\n    \
  \"ID\" -> \"RHUFT-C007\",\n      \"Claim\" -> \"The proton/electron mass \
ratio is given by \[CurlyPhi]^(15 + \[CurlyPhi]^-1) * (6455/6456).\",\n      \
\"Equation\" -> HoldForm[mp/me == \[CurlyPhi]^(15 + \[CurlyPhi]^-1) \
(6455/6456)],\n      \"Category\" -> \"NeedsEvidence\",\n      \"Type\" -> \
\"NumericalFit\",\n      \"RHUFTLayer\" -> \"Geometric Hierarchy\",\n      \
\"Rationale\" -> \"The numerical closeness is notable, but the correction \
factor is not currently derived from first principles.\",\n      \
\"Dependencies\" -> {\"Golden-ratio scaling law\", \"Meaning of 15\", \
\"Meaning of \[CurlyPhi]^-1 term\", \"Meaning of 6455/6456 correction\"},\n   \
   \"Evidence\" -> {\"High numerical agreement with measured mp/me\"},\n      \
\"ValidationPath\" -> {\"Derive each factor independently\", \"Test \
uniqueness\", \"Check predictive power on other observables\"},\n      \"Risk\
\" -> \"Post hoc fitting disguised as derivation.\",\n      \"NextAction\" -> \
\"Do not call proof; classify as candidate identity pending derivation.\"\n   \
|>,\n   <|\n      \"ID\" -> \"RHUFT-C008\",\n      \"Claim\" -> \"The \
fine-structure constant has an ideal geometric form 137 + \[Pi]^2/(6 e).\",\n \
     \"Equation\" -> HoldForm[1/\[Alpha]ideal == 137 + \[Pi]^2/(6 e)],\n      \
\"Category\" -> \"Speculative\",\n      \"Type\" -> \"Phenomenological\",\n   \
   \"RHUFTLayer\" -> \"Electromagnetic Boundary\",\n      \"Rationale\" -> \
\"This is an interesting ansatz, but it does not reproduce the empirical \
value closely enough to count as derivation.\",\n      \"Dependencies\" -> \
{\"Integer boundary 137\", \"\[Pi]/e correction mechanism\", \
\"Ideal-vs-measured separation\"},\n      \"Evidence\" -> {\"Uses \
mathematically meaningful constants\"},\n      \"ValidationPath\" -> \
{\"Derive from field-boundary condition\", \"Explain why this exact \
correction appears\", \"Test against renormalization-scale interpretation\"},\
\n      \"Risk\" -> \"Symbolic elegance mistaken for explanatory power.\",\n  \
    \"NextAction\" -> \"Reframe as an idealized ansatz, not as a validated \
law.\"\n   |>,\n   <|\n      \"ID\" -> \"RHUFT-C009\",\n      \"Claim\" -> \
\"The discrepancy between the geometric ideal and measured 1/\[Alpha] is an \
entropic non-coherence factor Cfluc.\",\n      \"Equation\" -> HoldForm[Cfluc \
== CIdeal/(1/\[Alpha]measured)],\n      \"Category\" -> \"NeedsEvidence\",\n  \
    \"Type\" -> \"Interpretive\",\n      \"RHUFTLayer\" -> \"Electromagnetic \
Boundary\",\n      \"Rationale\" -> \"Currently this reinterprets mismatch \
rather than deriving it dynamically.\",\n      \"Dependencies\" -> \
{\"Validity of ideal law\", \"Meaningful definition of entropy/coherence \
deviation\", \"Physical interpretation of ratio\"},\n      \"Evidence\" -> \
{\"A computable discrepancy ratio exists\"},\n      \"ValidationPath\" -> \
{\"Define entropy/coherence mathematically\", \"Derive why measured \[Alpha] \
should differ from ideal value\", \"Predict fluctuation behavior \
elsewhere\"},\n      \"Risk\" -> \"Turning residual error into a named \
constant without explanatory derivation.\",\n      \"NextAction\" -> \"Treat \
as a placeholder diagnostic, not yet as a physical constant.\"\n   |>,\n   <|\
\n      \"ID\" -> \"RHUFT-C010\",\n      \"Claim\" -> \"Stable particle \
states correspond to coherence-bounded geometric attractors or resonance \
nodes.\",\n      \"Equation\" -> \"Conceptual claim\",\n      \"Category\" -> \
\"Provisional\",\n      \"Type\" -> \"Interpretive\",\n      \"RHUFTLayer\" \
-> \"Stability and Actualization\",\n      \"Rationale\" -> \"Strongly \
aligned with the architecture and coherence narrative, but still requires \
explicit dynamical formulation.\",\n      \"Dependencies\" -> {\"Coherence \
field dynamics\", \"Boundary conditions\", \"Stability selection \
principle\"},\n      \"Evidence\" -> {\"Conceptually consistent with the old \
computational scaffold\"},\n      \"ValidationPath\" -> {\"Construct \
dynamical stability criterion\", \"Show localized attractors emerge under \
RHUFT evolution\"},\n      \"Risk\" -> \"May remain metaphorical unless \
operationalized.\",\n      \"NextAction\" -> \"Define a stability functional \
and solvable toy model.\"\n   |>,\n   <|\n      \"ID\" -> \"RHUFT-C011\",\n   \
   \"Claim\" -> \"The RHUFT master equation can be decomposed into \
dimensional, geometric-hierarchy, and boundary-condition factors.\",\n      \
\"Equation\" -> HoldForm[M == dimensionalFactor geometricFactor \
boundaryFactor],\n      \"Category\" -> \"Provisional\",\n      \"Type\" -> \
\"Structural\",\n      \"RHUFTLayer\" -> \"Master Synthesis\",\n      \
\"Rationale\" -> \"As a framework decomposition this is useful and coherent, \
even though individual factors are not equally established.\",\n      \
\"Dependencies\" -> {\"Mass emergence term\", \"Hierarchy term\", \"Boundary \
term\"},\n      \"Evidence\" -> {\"Clear conceptual modularity\"},\n      \
\"ValidationPath\" -> {\"Promote each factor individually toward derivation \
or downgrade it\"},\n      \"Risk\" -> \"Can appear more unified than \
justified if weak factors are embedded beside strong ones.\",\n      \
\"NextAction\" -> \"Keep the decomposition, but label factor confidence \
levels explicitly.\"\n   |>,\n   <|\n      \"ID\" -> \"RHUFT-C012\",\n      \
\"Claim\" -> \"RHUFT should distinguish exact derivations, structural \
ansatze, numerical fits, and interpretive overlays.\",\n      \"Equation\" -> \
\"Methodological principle\",\n      \"Category\" -> \"Derived\",\n      \
\"Type\" -> \"Methodological\",\n      \"RHUFTLayer\" -> \"Research \
Discipline\",\n      \"Rationale\" -> \"Necessary for professionalization and \
prevention of category errors.\",\n      \"Dependencies\" -> {\"Commitment to \
auditability and scientific clarity\"},\n      \"Evidence\" -> {\"Prevents \
overclaiming and improves theory development\"},\n      \"ValidationPath\" -> \
{\"Apply classification tags systematically to all RHUFT claims\"},\n      \
\"Risk\" -> \"Low; mostly organizational risk if not followed.\",\n      \
\"NextAction\" -> \"Adopt this as a formal RHUFT documentation policy.\"\n   \
|>\n};\n\nrhuftClaimAudit\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Summary by Category\n\n```wl\n\
Normal @ Counts[rhuftClaimAudit[All, \"Category\"] // Normal]\n```\n\n```wl\n\
claimCategorySummary = Dataset @ KeyValueMap[\n   <|\"Category\" -> #1, \
\"Count\" -> #2|> &,\n   Normal @ Counts[rhuftClaimAudit[All, \"Category\"] \
// Normal]\n];\n\nclaimCategorySummary\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Audit Utilities\n\
\n```wl\nClearAll[\n   claimsByCategory,\n   claimsByType,\n   claimsByLayer,\
\n   claimRiskRegister,\n   claimActionRegister,\n   claimDashboard\n];\n\n\
claimsByCategory[data_Dataset, category_String] :=\n   data[Select[#Category \
== category &]];\n\nclaimsByType[data_Dataset, type_String] :=\n   \
data[Select[#Type == type &]];\n\nclaimsByLayer[data_Dataset, layer_String] \
:=\n   data[Select[#RHUFTLayer == layer &]];\n\n\
claimRiskRegister[data_Dataset] :=\n   data[All, {\"ID\", \"Claim\", \
\"Category\", \"Risk\"}];\n\nclaimActionRegister[data_Dataset] :=\n   \
data[All, {\"ID\", \"Claim\", \"Category\", \"NextAction\"}];\n\n\
claimDashboard[data_Dataset] := Module[\n   {\n      categoryCounts,\n      \
barChart\n   },\n   categoryCounts = Counts[data[All, \"Category\"] // \
Normal];\n   barChart = BarChart[\n      Lookup[categoryCounts, \
claimStatusLevels, 0],\n      ChartLabels -> claimStatusLevels,\n      \
ChartStyle -> (claimStatusStyle /@ claimStatusLevels),\n      ImageSize -> \
Large,\n      PlotLabel -> \"RHUFT Claim Audit Overview\"\n   ];\n   Column[{\
\n      Style[\"RHUFT Claim Audit Dashboard\", 16, Bold],\n      barChart,\n  \
    Dataset @ KeyValueMap[\n         <|\"Category\" -> #1, \"Count\" -> #2|> \
&,\n         categoryCounts\n      ]\n   }]\n];\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Example \
Queries\n\n### Claims currently treated as Derived\n\n```wl\n\
claimsByCategory[rhuftClaimAudit, \"Derived\"]\n```\n\n### Claims that need \
evidence most urgently\n\n```wl\nclaimsByCategory[rhuftClaimAudit, \
\"NeedsEvidence\"]\n```\n\n### All numerical-fit style claims\n\n```wl\n\
claimsByType[rhuftClaimAudit, \"NumericalFit\"]\n```\n\n### Risk register\n\n\
```wl\nclaimRiskRegister[rhuftClaimAudit]\n```\n\n### Action register\n\n\
```wl\nclaimActionRegister[rhuftClaimAudit]\n```\n\n### Dashboard\n\n```wl\n\
claimDashboard[rhuftClaimAudit]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Professional Review \
Rules\n\n```wl\nreviewRules = Dataset @ {\n   <|\"Rule\" -> \"No dimensional \
result may be presented as a physical identity without additional derivation.\
\", \"Priority\" -> \"Critical\"|>,\n   <|\"Rule\" -> \"No numerical \
agreement may be called proof if correction factors are introduced post \
hoc.\", \"Priority\" -> \"Critical\"|>,\n   <|\"Rule\" -> \"All interpretive \
language must be separable from the underlying formal claim.\", \"Priority\" \
-> \"High\"|>,\n   <|\"Rule\" -> \"Every claim in RHUFT should have an \
explicit validation path.\", \"Priority\" -> \"High\"|>,\n   <|\"Rule\" -> \
\"Golden-ratio and geometric claims must be compared against alternative \
baselines.\", \"Priority\" -> \"High\"|>,\n   <|\"Rule\" -> \"Master \
equations must display factor confidence levels explicitly.\", \"Priority\" \
-> \"High\"|>\n};\n\nreviewRules\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Recommended Next \
Actions\n\n```wl\nnextProfessionalActions = Dataset @ {\n   <|\"Step\" -> 1, \
\"Action\" -> \"Formalize \[CapitalOmega] as a precise mathematical object \
with units, domain, and update law.\", \"Outcome\" -> \"Reduces ambiguity in \
the field foundation.\"|>,\n   <|\"Step\" -> 2, \"Action\" -> \"Rewrite the \
mass-emergence section to separate dimensional derivation from physical \
identification.\", \"Outcome\" -> \"Prevents overclaiming around G^-1.\"|>,\n \
  <|\"Step\" -> 3, \"Action\" -> \"Move the proton/electron ratio formula \
into a candidate-identity appendix until independently derived.\", \
\"Outcome\" -> \"Improves theoretical credibility.\"|>,\n   <|\"Step\" -> 4, \
\"Action\" -> \"Reframe the fine-structure discussion as an idealized ansatz \
plus residual diagnostic.\", \"Outcome\" -> \"Avoids treating mismatch as \
proof.\"|>,\n   <|\"Step\" -> 5, \"Action\" -> \"Create a companion \
validation notebook comparing RHUFT scaling claims against null and \
alternative models.\", \"Outcome\" -> \"Makes RHUFT ablation-ready and \
falsifiable.\"|>,\n   <|\"Step\" -> 6, \"Action\" -> \"Adopt this claim-audit \
dataset as the canonical governance layer for all future RHUFT revisions.\", \
\"Outcome\" -> \"Establishes professional documentation discipline.\"|>\n};\n\
\nnextProfessionalActions\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9. Optional Extension: Confidence \
Scores\n\n```wl\nClearAll[withConfidenceScore];\n\n\
withConfidenceScore[data_Dataset] := Dataset @ Map[\n   Append[\n      #,\n   \
   \"ConfidenceScore\" -> Switch[#Category,\n         \"Derived\", 0.9,\n     \
    \"Provisional\", 0.6,\n         \"Speculative\", 0.35,\n         \
\"NeedsEvidence\", 0.2,\n         _, Missing[\"Unknown\"]\n      ]\n   ] &,\n \
  Normal[data]\n];\n\nwithConfidenceScore[rhuftClaimAudit]\n```\n\n---\n\n## \
Closing Note\n\nThis notebook is designed to become the professional \
governance layer for RHUFT development.\n\nIts function is to ensure that \
RHUFT evolves with:\n\n- dimensional rigor,\n- claim traceability,\n- \
separation of derivation from interpretation,\n- numerical honesty,\n- and a \
clear validation roadmap.\n\nThe intended result is not merely a stronger \
document, but a stronger research program.\n\n/exec\nRESULT\n\
