  "CellToStringData" -> 
   "/create_nb\n# RHUFT Validation Notebook v1\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis notebook \
is the next professional stage after the claim-audit notebook. Its role is to \
convert RHUFT claims into a structured validation program with:\n\n- explicit \
test classes,\n- evidence standards,\n- falsification conditions,\n- \
reproducibility requirements,\n- and claim-to-test mappings.\n\nThe goal is \
to work slowly, accurately, and properly by separating:\n\n1. what can be \
checked immediately,\n2. what requires formal derivation,\n3. what requires \
comparative modeling,\n4. and what currently remains interpretive.\n\n---\n\n\
## 1. Validation Categories\n\n```wl\nClearAll[\n  validationClasses,\n  \
evidenceLevels,\n  validationStatuses,\n  validationClassStyle,\n  \
evidenceLevelOrder\n];\n\nvalidationClasses = {\n  \"Dimensional\",\n  \
\"Symbolic\",\n  \"Numerical\",\n  \"Comparative\",\n  \"Empirical\",\n  \
\"Interpretive\"\n};\n\nevidenceLevels = {\n  \"ImmediateCheck\",\n  \
\"FormalDerivation\",\n  \"SimulationStudy\",\n  \"ComparativeBenchmark\",\n  \
\"ExternalMeasurement\"\n};\n\nvalidationStatuses = {\n  \"NotStarted\",\n  \
\"Planned\",\n  \"InProgress\",\n  \"PartiallySupported\",\n  \"Validated\",\n\
  \"Failed\",\n  \"Inconclusive\"\n};\n\nevidenceLevelOrder = \
AssociationThread[evidenceLevels, Range[Length[evidenceLevels]]];\n\n\
validationClassStyle = <|\n  \"Dimensional\" -> Darker[Blue, 0.2],\n  \
\"Symbolic\" -> Purple,\n  \"Numerical\" -> Darker[Green, 0.2],\n  \
\"Comparative\" -> RGBColor[0.8, 0.45, 0.1],\n  \"Empirical\" -> \
RGBColor[0.75, 0.2, 0.2],\n  \"Interpretive\" -> GrayLevel[0.35]\n|>;\n```\n\n\
---\n\n## 2. Validation Schema\n\n```wl\nClearAll[rhuftValidationSchema];\n\n\
rhuftValidationSchema = {\n  \"ClaimID\",\n  \"Claim\",\n  \"AuditCategory\",\
\n  \"ValidationClass\",\n  \"EvidenceLevel\",\n  \"TestName\",\n  \
\"TestQuestion\",\n  \"PassCriterion\",\n  \"FailCriterion\",\n  \
\"InputsNeeded\",\n  \"Method\",\n  \"Dependencies\",\n  \"Status\",\n  \
\"Priority\",\n  \"Notes\"\n};\n\nrhuftValidationSchema\n```\n\n### Field \
meanings\n\n- `ClaimID`: link to the claim-audit notebook\n- `Claim`: short \
version of the claim being validated\n- `AuditCategory`: current audit \
category from the claim register\n- `ValidationClass`: dimensional, symbolic, \
numerical, comparative, empirical, or interpretive\n- `EvidenceLevel`: \
smallest level of evidence needed for progress\n- `TestName`: concise test \
label\n- `TestQuestion`: exact question being asked\n- `PassCriterion`: what \
would count as support\n- `FailCriterion`: what would count as failure\n- \
`InputsNeeded`: formulas, data, constants, simulations, etc.\n- `Method`: \
validation approach\n- `Dependencies`: what must already be defined\n- \
`Status`: current test status\n- `Priority`: professional urgency ranking\n- \
`Notes`: comments or caveats\n\n---\n\n## 3. Initial Validation Register\n\n\
```wl\nClearAll[rhuftValidationRegister];\n\nrhuftValidationRegister = \
Dataset @ {\n  <|\n    \"ClaimID\" -> \"RHUFT-C001\",\n    \"Claim\" -> \"\
\[CapitalOmega] can be defined as a recursive coherence rate with dimensions \
T^-1.\",\n    \"AuditCategory\" -> \"Provisional\",\n    \"ValidationClass\" \
-> \"Dimensional\",\n    \"EvidenceLevel\" -> \"FormalDerivation\",\n    \
\"TestName\" -> \"OmegaDimensionalClosure\",\n    \"TestQuestion\" -> \"Does \
assigning T^-1 to \[CapitalOmega] remove dimensional inconsistencies in all \
RHUFT kernel expressions?\",\n    \"PassCriterion\" -> \"Every kernel \
argument involving \[CapitalOmega] is dimensionless under a single consistent \
unit assignment.\",\n    \"FailCriterion\" -> \"At least one core RHUFT \
expression remains dimensionally inconsistent under the assignment [\
\[CapitalOmega]] = T^-1.\",\n    \"InputsNeeded\" -> {\"All RHUFT field \
equations\", \"Kernel definitions\", \"Unit assumptions\"},\n    \"Method\" \
-> \"Full dimensional audit of all expressions containing \[CapitalOmega].\",\
\n    \"Dependencies\" -> {\"Canonical RHUFT equation list\"},\n    \
\"Status\" -> \"Planned\",\n    \"Priority\" -> \"Critical\",\n    \"Notes\" \
-> \"This is foundational because downstream equations depend on \
\[CapitalOmega] being well-defined.\"\n  |>,\n  <|\n    \"ClaimID\" -> \
\"RHUFT-C002\",\n    \"Claim\" -> \"Recursive exponential kernel arguments \
must be dimensionless.\",\n    \"AuditCategory\" -> \"Derived\",\n    \
\"ValidationClass\" -> \"Dimensional\",\n    \"EvidenceLevel\" -> \
\"ImmediateCheck\",\n    \"TestName\" -> \"ExponentialArgumentRule\",\n    \
\"TestQuestion\" -> \"Do RHUFT exponential arguments satisfy the standard \
dimensionless requirement?\",\n    \"PassCriterion\" -> \"All exponential \
arguments are dimensionless.\",\n    \"FailCriterion\" -> \"Any exponential \
argument carries units.\",\n    \"InputsNeeded\" -> {\"Exponential terms in \
RHUFT\"},\n    \"Method\" -> \"Manual and symbolic dimensional inspection.\",\
\n    \"Dependencies\" -> {\"Canonical expression list\"},\n    \"Status\" -> \
\"Planned\",\n    \"Priority\" -> \"Critical\",\n    \"Notes\" -> \"This is a \
universal mathematical consistency requirement, not RHUFT-specific.\"\n  |>,\n\
  <|\n    \"ClaimID\" -> \"RHUFT-C003\",\n    \"Claim\" -> \"Mass can be \
modeled as an integrated coherence-contrast functional.\",\n    \
\"AuditCategory\" -> \"Provisional\",\n    \"ValidationClass\" -> \
\"Symbolic\",\n    \"EvidenceLevel\" -> \"FormalDerivation\",\n    \"TestName\
\" -> \"MassFunctionalJustification\",\n    \"TestQuestion\" -> \"Can the \
proposed mass functional be derived from a RHUFT stability principle, action \
principle, or conservation law?\",\n    \"PassCriterion\" -> \"A principled \
derivation uniquely or preferentially selects the coherence-contrast \
functional.\",\n    \"FailCriterion\" -> \"The functional remains an \
unsupported modeling choice among many equally plausible alternatives.\",\n   \
 \"InputsNeeded\" -> {\"Mass functional\", \"Candidate variational \
principle\", \"RHUFT dynamics\"},\n    \"Method\" -> \"Derivation attempt \
plus alternative-functional comparison.\",\n    \"Dependencies\" -> \
{\"Precise definition of \[CapitalOmega]\", \"Background field definition\"},\
\n    \"Status\" -> \"Planned\",\n    \"Priority\" -> \"High\",\n    \
\"Notes\" -> \"This should not be overstated unless derivation or unique \
preference is established.\"\n  |>,\n  <|\n    \"ClaimID\" -> \"RHUFT-C004\",\
\n    \"Claim\" -> \"The coupling coefficient in the mass functional has \
dimensions matching G^-1.\",\n    \"AuditCategory\" -> \"Derived\",\n    \
\"ValidationClass\" -> \"Dimensional\",\n    \"EvidenceLevel\" -> \
\"ImmediateCheck\",\n    \"TestName\" -> \"GInverseDimensionalMatch\",\n    \
\"TestQuestion\" -> \"Does the proposed mass functional require a coefficient \
with dimensions equal to G^-1?\",\n    \"PassCriterion\" -> \"Dimensional \
analysis yields M L^-3 T^2, exactly matching [G^-1].\",\n    \
\"FailCriterion\" -> \"Dimensional analysis does not match [G^-1].\",\n    \
\"InputsNeeded\" -> {\"Mass functional\", \"Dimensions of \[CapitalOmega]\", \
\"Volume element dimensions\", \"Dimensions of G\"},\n    \"Method\" -> \
\"Explicit symbolic dimensional derivation.\",\n    \"Dependencies\" -> \
