rhuftValidationRegister\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Validation Utilities\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[\n  validationsByStatus,\n  validationsByPriority,\n  \
validationsByClass,\n  validationsByClaim,\n  validationActionTable,\n  \
validationSummary\n];\n\nvalidationsByStatus[data_Dataset, status_String] :=\n\
  data[Select[#Status == status &]];\n\nvalidationsByPriority[data_Dataset, \
priority_String] :=\n  data[Select[#Priority == priority &]];\n\n\
validationsByClass[data_Dataset, class_String] :=\n  \
data[Select[#ValidationClass == class &]];\n\n\
validationsByClaim[data_Dataset, claimID_String] :=\n  data[Select[#ClaimID \
== claimID &]];\n\nvalidationActionTable[data_Dataset] :=\n  data[All, \
{\"ClaimID\", \"TestName\", \"Priority\", \"Status\", \"Method\"}];\n\n\
validationSummary[data_Dataset] := Dataset @ {\n  <|\"Field\" -> \"TotalTests\
\", \"Value\" -> Length[Normal[data]]|>,\n  <|\"Field\" -> \"CriticalPriority\
\", \"Value\" -> Count[data[All, \"Priority\"] // Normal, \"Critical\"]|>,\n  \
<|\"Field\" -> \"HighPriority\", \"Value\" -> Count[data[All, \"Priority\"] \
// Normal, \"High\"]|>,\n  <|\"Field\" -> \"Planned\", \"Value\" -> \
Count[data[All, \"Status\"] // Normal, \"Planned\"]|>\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n## \
5. Immediate Critical Queue\n\n```wl\ncriticalQueue = \
validationsByPriority[rhuftValidationRegister, \"Critical\"];\ncriticalQueue\n\
```\n\nThese are the first items that should be resolved before expanding \
speculative sections.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Professional Validation Rules\n\n```wl\n\
validationRules = Dataset @ {\n  <|\"Rule\" -> \"No dimensional result is to \
be presented as physical identity without additional derivation.\", \
\"Priority\" -> \"Critical\"|>,\n  <|\"Rule\" -> \"No numerical match is to \
be called proof if any correction term is post hoc or weakly justified.\", \
\"Priority\" -> \"Critical\"|>,\n  <|\"Rule\" -> \"Every claim must specify \
pass and fail conditions.\", \"Priority\" -> \"Critical\"|>,\n  <|\"Rule\" -> \
\"Comparative claims must be benchmarked against declared alternative models.\
\", \"Priority\" -> \"High\"|>,\n  <|\"Rule\" -> \"Interpretive language must \
not substitute for a derivation.\", \"Priority\" -> \"High\"|>,\n  <|\"Rule\" \
-> \"All validation work must be reproducible from explicit constants, code, \
and assumptions.\", \"Priority\" -> \"Critical\"|>\n};\n\nvalidationRules\n\
```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Stage Plan\n\n```wl\nvalidationStagePlan = Dataset @ {\n  \
<|\"Stage\" -> 1, \"Name\" -> \"Canonical Equation Audit\", \"Goal\" -> \
\"Collect the exact RHUFT equations to be validated.\", \"Deliverable\" -> \
\"Equation register with unit annotations.\"|>,\n  <|\"Stage\" -> 2, \"Name\" \
-> \"Dimensional Validation\", \"Goal\" -> \"Check all core equations for \
dimensional consistency.\", \"Deliverable\" -> \"Dimensional report with \
pass/fail outcomes.\"|>,\n  <|\"Stage\" -> 3, \"Name\" -> \"Derivation \
Audit\", \"Goal\" -> \"Separate derivations from ansatze and fits.\", \
\"Deliverable\" -> \"Provenance map for every major formula.\"|>,\n  \
<|\"Stage\" -> 4, \"Name\" -> \"Comparative Model Testing\", \"Goal\" -> \
\"Benchmark geometric and scaling claims against alternatives.\", \
\"Deliverable\" -> \"Comparative metrics and selection criteria.\"|>,\n  \
<|\"Stage\" -> 5, \"Name\" -> \"Toy Dynamics Validation\", \"Goal\" -> \"Test \
whether RHUFT-like dynamics actually yield stable coherent structures.\", \
\"Deliverable\" -> \"Simulation notebook and stability report.\"|>,\n  \
<|\"Stage\" -> 6, \"Name\" -> \"Integrated Validation Report\", \"Goal\" -> \
\"Summarize validated, unresolved, and unsupported claims.\", \"Deliverable\" \
-> \"Formal RHUFT validation report.\"|>\n};\n\nvalidationStagePlan\n```\n\n\
---\n\n## 8. Recommended Immediate Work Order\n\n```wl\nimmediateWorkOrder = \
Dataset @ {\n  <|\"Order\" -> 1, \"Task\" -> \"Create a canonical equation \
register from the current RHUFT text.\", \"Reason\" -> \"Validation cannot \
proceed reliably without a fixed source of equations.\"|>,\n  <|\"Order\" -> \
2, \"Task\" -> \"Run dimensional checks on \[CapitalOmega] definitions, \
kernel arguments, and the mass functional.\", \"Reason\" -> \"These are the \
strongest and most foundational claims.\"|>,\n  <|\"Order\" -> 3, \"Task\" -> \
\"Perform provenance audit on mp/me and 1/\[Alpha] formulas.\", \"Reason\" -> \
\"Need to distinguish prediction from fit before using these formulas \
rhetorically.\"|>,\n  <|\"Order\" -> 4, \"Task\" -> \"Define a minimal \
executable toy model for stable coherent-node emergence.\", \"Reason\" -> \
\"Connect conceptual RHUFT language to explicit dynamics.\"|>\n};\n\n\
immediateWorkOrder\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9. Closing Note\n\nThis notebook is \
intentionally procedural and conservative.\n\nIts purpose is to ensure that \
RHUFT develops with:\n\n- explicit validation logic,\n- clean separation of \
derivation from interpretation,\n- reproducible standards,\n- and a \
disciplined path from concept to tested structure.\n\nThe next operational \
step after this notebook is:\n\n**Stage 1: build the canonical RHUFT equation \
register**, then begin dimensional validation from that register.\n\n/exec\n\
